---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-resizable-panels</code> is a split view: its <code>wc-panel</code> children sit side by
  side with a divider between each pair, and dragging a divider resizes the two panels beside it.
  A panel's <code>size</code> is its share in percent; panels without one share what is left.
  <code>min-size</code> and <code>max-size</code> bound the size. Each panel scrolls its own
  content. In right-to-left layouts horizontal drags mirror.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-resizable-panels
    id='resizable-panels-demo'
    style='height: 320px; border: 1px solid var(--color-outline-variant); border-radius: 1rem;'
  >
    <wc-panel size='30' min-size='20' max-size='50' label='Messages'>
      <div style='padding: 1rem;'>Messages</div>
    </wc-panel>
    <wc-panel min-size='30' label='Message'>
      <div style='padding: 1rem;'>Message</div>
    </wc-panel>
  </wc-resizable-panels>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#resizable-panels-demo').addEventListener('change', function (event) {
      myConsole.log('change: ' + event.detail.value.join(', '));
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Vertical and nested</h3>
<p>
  <code>orientation="vertical"</code> stacks the panels. A panel can hold another split view, for
  an editor beside a preview above a console.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-resizable-panels
    style='height: 360px; border: 1px solid var(--color-outline-variant); border-radius: 1rem;'
  >
    <wc-panel size='50' min-size='20' label='Editor'>
      <div style='padding: 1rem;'>Editor</div>
    </wc-panel>
    <wc-panel label='Output'>
      <wc-resizable-panels orientation='vertical'>
        <wc-panel size='60' label='Preview'>
          <div style='padding: 1rem;'>Preview</div>
        </wc-panel>
        <wc-panel min-size='15' label='Console'>
          <div style='padding: 1rem;'>Console</div>
        </wc-panel>
      </wc-resizable-panels>
    </wc-panel>
  </wc-resizable-panels>
</DemoComponentCard>
